<p>US military investigators have tentatively concluded that US forces were likely responsible for an apparent strike that hit a girls’ school in Minab, southern Iran, killing large numbers of children, according to two US officials cited by Reuters. The officials stressed the inquiry is not finished, and that new evidence could still change that assessment. The strike happened on the first day of US and Israeli attacks on Iran, and Iranian officials say the toll is far higher than what independent reporting has been able to confirm so far. Separate reporting and analysis suggested the school may have been hit during strikes on an adjacent Iranian naval base, raising the possibility it was struck as part of a nearby military operation. Visual reporting and video analysis from the scene have also pointed to extensive civilian harm, including children, intensifying scrutiny and adding urgency to calls for accountability and stronger protections for civilians in the conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GLgKOY8Kxv6JyUbEq8s4N6zhSP0btLhw4PL8-DhIPKc9C3bjaJtsY44XxZVmRgCDFxaV9N7bPHBdwOMIh9GiuArfi89cxbgBYXrHM11e_UH1tzp8pTSXVG3bJhEVuB-J7yjxrn84Az6Pn8gu0GDAd_3iTurFAGJ47yK5bXYhkaNGHIBH8tJ_OTzMJ64RoAsfhEYa2P_qSj610dzDKhoDkhsB7SRNQdGu63I_30Podp4hvx8mSRjhYIxIExFMQCQo7MtApPp_THmPKPBqhA' alt='Graves are prepared for victims following a reported strike on a school in Minab, Iran, March 2, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>US response: US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said in a Wednesday briefing that the military is investigating the incident.</li><li>Iran claim: Iran’s ambassador to the UN in Geneva, Ali Bahreini, said the strike killed 150 students — a figure Reuters said it could not independently verify.</li><li>Contextual analysis: The New York Times reported its analysis suggests the strike was linked to attacks on a nearby Iranian naval base where officials said US forces were operating.</li><li>Scene evidence: Le Monde said it verified videos showing many civilian victims, including children, at the Minab school site.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US military investigators (via officials): Two US officials cited by Reuters said investigators currently see US forces as the likely source of the strike, but emphasized the assessment is tentative and could change as more evidence emerges. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/exclusive-us-investigation-points-likely-us-responsibility-iran-school-strike'>Al-Monitor (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Iranian government (UN mission): Iran’s ambassador in Geneva, Ali Bahreini, blamed the attacking forces and said 150 students were killed, a figure Reuters said it could not independently verify, while pointing to the broader hostilities between Iran and the US-Israel coalition. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979015/us-investigation-points-to-likely-us-responsibility-in-iran-school-strike-sources-say'>Dawn (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>White House: Press secretary Karoline Leavitt said an investigation is underway while arguing the Iranian regime — not the US — targets civilians and children. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979015/us-investigation-points-to-likely-us-responsibility-in-iran-school-strike-sources-say'>Dawn (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>The New York Times (visual analysis): The paper reported the strike appears to have happened during attacks on an adjacent naval base, suggesting the school was hit in the course of a nearby military operation. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/05/world/middleeast/iran-school-us-strikes-naval-base.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde (video investigation): Le Monde reported it obtained and analyzed videos that it said show many civilian victims, including children, after the bombing of the Minab school. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/videos/article/2026/03/06/iranian-school-hit-by-air-strike-le-monde-s-investigation-confirms-many-civilian-victims-including-children_6751145_108.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3345645/us-seen-likely-responsible-iran-school-strike-killed-scores-children'>US seen as likely responsible for Iran school strike that killed scores of children</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979015/us-investigation-points-to-likely-us-responsibility-in-iran-school-strike-sources-say'>US investigation points to likely US responsibility in Iran school strike, sources say</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-war-school-strike-us/'>Investigation suggests U.S. military likely responsible for Iran school strike, sources say</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/exclusive-us-investigation-points-likely-us-responsibility-iran-school-strike'>Exclusive-US investigation points to likely US responsibility in Iran school strike, sources say</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/05/world/middleeast/iran-school-us-strikes-naval-base.html'>Analysis Suggests School Was Hit Amid U.S. Strikes on Iranian Naval Base</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/videos/article/2026/03/06/iranian-school-hit-by-air-strike-le-monde-s-investigation-confirms-many-civilian-victims-including-children_6751145_108.html'>Iranian school hit by air strike: Le Monde&#x27;s investigation confirms many civilian victims, including children</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-investigation-points-to-likely-us-responsibility-in-iran-school-strike-sources-say'>US investigation points to likely US responsibility in Iran girls’ school strike</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>